% Seat Lift Mechanisms: LCD L33801 and its Policy Article A52518 (DME MACs),
% read with NCD 280.4 (seat lift). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it
% includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need,
% refills) and states when a claim for a seat lift mechanism — electric
% (E0627) or manual (E0629) — is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the clinical
% criteria (severe arthritis of the hip or knee or a severe neuromuscular
% disease; part of the practitioner's course of treatment; completely
% incapable of standing up from a regular chair; able to ambulate once
% standing), the type of mechanism (smooth, controlled by the beneficiary,
% effective without other assistance, not a spring-release catapult), the
% ordering practitioner, and the record of the therapeutic modalities tried.
% Only the mechanism is in the benefit: a lift chair sold as a unit is billed
% as the mechanism (E0627 or E0629) and the chair as A9270, which has no
% benefit category (the Policy Article's coding guidelines); a toilet seat
% lift (E0172) is non-covered. Both are in scope, with no benefit.
%
% How the criteria are read. The LCD's clinical criteria are findings about
% the beneficiary made by the treating practitioner and accepted or rejected
% on review: each is the judged template of dmepos.le, "the finding F about
% B is established" (or unsupported), with who found it and why. Where the
% LCD offers alternatives (arthritis of the hip, arthritis of the knee, a
% neuromuscular disease) they are ONE finding with the alternative as its
% reason. The findings this policy reads, and the criterion each stands for:
%   qualifying seat lift diagnosis (1: severe arthritis of the hip or knee,
%   or a severe neuromuscular disease — the NCD names muscular dystrophy);
%   seat lift part of course of treatment (2: part of the treating
%   practitioner's course of treatment, prescribed to effect improvement or
%   arrest or retard deterioration — the NCD's "can benefit
%   therapeutically"); completely incapable of standing from any chair (3:
%   from a regular armchair or any chair in the home — difficulty, or a low
%   chair, is not enough); able to ambulate once standing (4).
% What the record states as fact — how the mechanism operates, who wrote the
% order, that the practitioner's record documents the therapeutic modalities
% tried and failed, the certificate of medical necessity of an old claim — is
% a scenario fact.
%
% The payment condition the policy adds (Policy Article A52518, "Certificate
% of medical necessity"): for a date of service before 1 January 2023 the
% CMN (CMS Form 849), completed, signed and dated by the treating
% practitioner, must be on file; from that date no CMN is needed. Not
% modelled: the KX/GA/GZ modifiers; the NCD's limit of the payment for a unit
% with a recliner feature to the amount payable for a seat lift without it
% (the model decides coverage, not amounts); the NCD's "the alternative would
% be chair or bed confinement", read as the reason behind criteria 3 and 4.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *an item* operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary; undefined.
    *an item* effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance; undefined.
    *an item* operates by a spring release mechanism; undefined.
    the order for *an item* was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition; undefined.
    the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    the supplier holds a completed certificate of medical necessity for *an item* signed by the treating practitioner; undefined.
    % derived
    *an item* is a seat lift mechanism.
    *a beneficiary* meets the clinical criteria for a seat lift mechanism.
    *an item* is an acceptable type of seat lift mechanism.
    *a claim* needs a certificate of medical necessity.

the knowledge base seat lifts includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base seat lifts includes:

LCD L33801 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33801".
the text of LCD L33801 is at "sources/lcd/L33801.txt".
Policy Article A52518 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52518".
the text of Policy Article A52518 is at "sources/article/A52518.txt".
NCD 280 4 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/ncd.aspx?ncdid=64".
the text of NCD 280 4 is at "sources/ncd/NCD_280.4.txt".

% What a seat lift mechanism is (the Policy Article's coding guidelines).
rule seat_lift_mechanism with provenance Policy Article A52518,
        confer "A seat lift mechanism that is electrically operated is billed using HCPCS code E0627. A manually operated seat lift mechanism is billed using HCPCS code E0629":
an item is a seat lift mechanism
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0627", "E0629"].

% A claim dated before 1 January 2023 needs the certificate of medical
% necessity (CMS Form 849).
rule seat_lifts_cmn_period with provenance Policy Article A52518,
        confer "For claims with dates of service prior to January 1, 2023 – If the CMN or DIF is required, it must be submitted with the claim, or be on file with a previous claim":
a claim needs a certificate of medical necessity
    if the policy of the claim is seat_lifts
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the date is before 2023-01-01.

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides: the mechanisms, the chair billed with them
% (A9270) and the toilet seat lift (E0172); the benefit — durable medical
% equipment — is the mechanism's alone.
rule seat_lifts_codes with provenance Policy Article A52518,
        confer "the supplier may bill the seat lift mechanism using E0627 or E0629, and bill A9270 for the chair":
the policy for code a code is seat_lifts
    if the code is in ["E0627", "E0629", "E0172", "A9270"].

rule seat_lifts_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52518,
        confer "Seat lift mechanisms are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the code is in ["E0627", "E0629"].

section question is:

% The mechanism is covered if all the criteria are met: the clinical
% criteria, the type, the ordering practitioner, the record of the
% modalities tried.
rule seat_lifts_covered with provenance LCD L33801,
        confer "A seat lift mechanism is covered if all of the following criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a seat lift mechanism
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the clinical criteria for a seat lift mechanism
    and the item is an acceptable type of seat lift mechanism
    and the order for the item was written by the treating practitioner or a consulting practitioner for the condition
    and the record of the treating practitioner documents that all appropriate therapeutic modalities were tried and failed for the beneficiary.

% The clinical criteria: the findings of the treating practitioner.
rule seat_lifts_clinical_criteria with provenance LCD L33801,
        confer "The beneficiary must have severe arthritis of the hip or knee or have a severe neuromuscular disease":
a beneficiary meets the clinical criteria for a seat lift mechanism
    if the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding able to ambulate once standing about the beneficiary is established.

% The type of mechanism: smooth, controlled by the beneficiary, effective
% without other assistance; not the spring-release catapult.
rule seat_lifts_type with provenance NCD 280 4,
        confer "Coverage of seat lifts is limited to those types which operate smoothly, can be controlled by the patient, and effectively assist a patient in standing up and sitting down without other assistance":
an item is an acceptable type of seat lift mechanism
    if the item operates smoothly under the control of the beneficiary
    and the item effectively assists the beneficiary in standing up and sitting down without other assistance
    and it is not the case that
        the item operates by a spring release mechanism.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own condition of payment: the certificate of medical
% necessity of a claim dated before 2023.
rule seat_lifts_cmn with provenance Policy Article A52518,
        confer "For dates of service for which a CMN is required, a CMN, which has been completed, signed and dated by the treating practitioner, must be kept on file by the supplier, and made available upon request":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim needs a certificate of medical necessity
    and the claim is for an item
    and the supplier holds a completed certificate of medical necessity for the item signed by the treating practitioner.

rule seat_lifts_no_cmn with provenance Policy Article A52518,
        confer "Providers and suppliers no longer need to submit Certificate of Medical Necessity (CMN) for services rendered on or after January 1, 2023":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is seat_lifts
    and it is not the case that
        the claim needs a certificate of medical necessity.
